<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sadyattes</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">7th century BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century-bce">7th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sadyattes was a king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lydia">Lydia</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mermnad-dynasty">Mermnad dynasty</a>, son of Ardys and father of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alyattes">Alyattes</a>, who reigned in the later 7th century BCE from his capital at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sardis">Sardis</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/herodotus">Herodotus</a> records that he began the long war against Miletus, invading its territory every year at harvest time to burn the crops, a war that his son continued until peace was made with the tyrant Thrasybulus.</p></div>
